## What was carried over

- The three-paragraph aim-prompt skeleton (originated by Matt Shumer;
  packaged as a slash-command skill by duolahypercho).
- The "do not invent" anti-pattern list.
- The `compose only` opt-out.

## What was rewritten

- Host retarget: Claude Code + Codex → opencode.
- Fictional verbs (`/loop`, `/goal`, `ultracode`) removed.
- Rhetorical fan-out / critic / blind-compare rewired to real opencode
  primitives (`task()` with categories/subagents, `oracle`, `visual-qa`,
  `playwright`, `background_output`).
- Install model: per-project drop-in, never global.
- Compose-only is the default; `--run` is opt-in.
